Z||000000||Runner||05-28-2000||02:57 PM||||I have an 86 SE 2M6 with 26,000 original KMS (15,000 miles).  When I first bought the car the clutch engaged closer to the floor or midway in the clutch cycle.  Of late the clutch seem to have made a significnat change and now engages at the very top end of the stroke.  I have checked the hydraulics and everything seems to be fine.<BR>Any ideas on why this would happen?  Should I be concerned?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||05-28-2000||03:20 PM||||It sounds like you've got the ever-famous bent aluminum clutch petal... Get the steel one from GM or <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||05-28-2000||03:59 PM||||If you had problems disengaging the clutch (i.e., grinding between shifts, clutch grabbing very close to the floor), then I would suspect a hydraulic problem, bent clutch fork or bent clutch pedal.  However, engagement seems to be your problem.  It sounds like your clutch plate may be worn and nearing end-of-life.  Have you noticed any slipping in high gear?||||reg||1
